1006
01:11:06.812 --> 01:11:08.747
♪ ♪

1007
01:11:28.834 --> 01:11:30.769
♪ ♪

1008
01:11:36.308 --> 01:11:37.974
- (gunshot)
- (Schofield grunts)

1009
01:11:37.976 --> 01:11:39.911
(panting)

1010
01:11:56.061 --> 01:11:58.263
(man shouts in German)

1011
01:12:02.234 --> 01:12:04.234
(panting)

1012
01:12:04.236 --> 01:12:06.204
(footsteps running past)

1013
01:12:26.258 --> 01:12:28.226
♪ ♪

1014
01:12:45.511 --> 01:12:47.346
(breathing shakily)

1015
01:12:53.118 --> 01:12:54.984
SCHOFIELD:
<i>Anglais.</i>

1016
01:12:54.986 --> 01:12:56.986
Not German.

1017
01:12:56.988 --> 01:12:58.456
Friend.

1018
01:12:58.458 --> 01:13:00.256
I'm a friend.

1019
01:13:00.258 --> 01:13:03.193
(sets down rifle)

1020
01:13:03.195 --> 01:13:06.162
This place. this town.

1021
01:13:06.164 --> 01:13:08.264
Écoust?

1022
01:13:08.266 --> 01:13:09.402
<i>C'est Écoust?</i>

1023
01:13:11.471 --> 01:13:13.038
(Schofield sighs)

1024
01:13:17.242 --> 01:13:19.109
Others?

1025
01:13:19.111 --> 01:13:20.879
No. Just me.

1026
01:13:22.948 --> 01:13:25.016
O-Only me.

1027
01:13:28.019 --> 01:13:31.020
I need to be somewhere.

1028
01:13:31.022 --> 01:13:34.025
I need to find a wood
to the southeast.

1029
01:13:36.094 --> 01:13:37.994
Uh. trees.

1030
01:13:37.996 --> 01:13:39.898
<i>Les arbres?</i>

1031
01:13:41.967 --> 01:13:44.334
- Uh. Croiset?
- Croisilles?

1032
01:13:44.336 --> 01:13:46.071
Yes.

1033
01:13:49.509 --> 01:13:52.342
- River.
- River.

1034
01:13:52.344 --> 01:13:55.078
It go there.

1035
01:13:55.080 --> 01:13:56.212
Trees.

1036
01:13:56.214 --> 01:13:59.182
Croisilles.

1037
01:13:59.184 --> 01:14:01.186
(Schofield groans)

1038
01:14:04.757 --> 01:14:06.224
(groans softly)

1039
01:14:09.060 --> 01:14:10.295
(grunts)

1040
01:14:13.298 --> 01:14:15.233
<i>Asseyez-vous. monsieur.</i>

1041
01:14:19.439 --> 01:14:21.373
(panting)

1042
01:14:28.514 --> 01:14:30.182
(groans)

1043
01:14:34.520 --> 01:14:37.322
(shushing)

1044
01:14:58.343 --> 01:14:59.412
(gasps)

1045
01:15:01.380 --> 01:15:02.582
(exhales sharply)

1046
01:15:15.528 --> 01:15:17.497
(sighing)

1047
01:15:30.075 --> 01:15:31.410
Thank you.

1048
01:15:32.612 --> 01:15:34.547
(baby fussing quietly)

1049
01:15:38.149 --> 01:15:39.385
(exhales sharply)

1050
01:15:43.589 --> 01:15:45.558
(baby continues
fussing quietly)

1051
01:15:59.237 --> 01:16:00.406
SCHOFIELD:
A girl?

1052
01:16:11.249 --> 01:16:13.184
(baby continues
fussing quietly)

1053
01:16:18.457 --> 01:16:20.225
What is her name?

1054
01:16:24.463 --> 01:16:26.399
Who is her mother?

1055
01:16:35.140 --> 01:16:38.141
I have food.

1056
01:16:38.143 --> 01:16:39.344
Here.

1057
01:16:42.481 --> 01:16:45.348
I have these.

1058
01:16:45.350 --> 01:16:46.617
But you can have them.

1059
01:16:46.619 --> 01:16:48.485
Here. take them all.

1060
01:16:48.487 --> 01:16:50.153
For you and the child.

1061
01:16:50.155 --> 01:16:51.356
Here.

1062
01:17:01.634 --> 01:17:03.234
Milk?

1063
01:17:14.447 --> 01:17:15.648
(sniffs)

1064
01:17:23.389 --> 01:17:24.624
<i>Merci.</i>

1065
01:17:32.732 --> 01:17:34.299
<i>Bonjour.</i>

1066
01:17:36.368 --> 01:17:37.703
- <i>Bonjour.</i>
- (baby fusses)

1067
01:17:41.674 --> 01:17:43.272
Children?

1068
01:17:43.274 --> 01:17:45.409
- You?
- (baby fusses)

1069
01:17:45.411 --> 01:17:47.243
(shushes)

1070
01:17:47.245 --> 01:17:49.180
- It's all right.
- (baby quiets)

1071
01:17:55.454 --> 01:17:56.689
(speaks French)

1072
01:18:03.294 --> 01:18:06.597
"They went to sea in a Sieve.
they did.

1073
01:18:06.599 --> 01:18:10.266
"In a Sieve they went to sea:

1074
01:18:10.268 --> 01:18:13.570
"In spite of
all their friends could say.

1075
01:18:13.572 --> 01:18:17.374
"On a winter's morn.
on a stormy day.

1076
01:18:17.376 --> 01:18:20.577
"In a Sieve they went to sea!

1077
01:18:20.579 --> 01:18:23.714
"Far and few. far and few.

1078
01:18:23.716 --> 01:18:27.718
"Are the lands
where the Jumblies live;

1079
01:18:27.720 --> 01:18:31.457
"Their heads are green.
and their hands are blue.

1080
01:18:33.859 --> 01:18:36.261
And they went to sea
in a Sieve."

1081
01:18:40.866 --> 01:18:44.804
(church bell tolling slowly
six times in distance)

1082
01:18:48.874 --> 01:18:50.810
♪ ♪

1083
01:19:00.786 --> 01:19:02.353
(baby coos)

1084
01:19:13.666 --> 01:19:15.233
(baby fussing quietly)

1085
01:19:22.742 --> 01:19:24.742
- (pained grunt)
- Stay.

1086
01:19:24.744 --> 01:19:25.876
Stay.

1087
01:19:25.878 --> 01:19:27.310
Please.

1088
01:19:27.312 --> 01:19:29.247
I have to go.

1089
01:19:36.354 --> 01:19:38.354
(baby fussing quietly)

1090
01:19:38.356 --> 01:19:39.389
Please.

1091
01:19:39.391 --> 01:19:41.359
I'm sorry.

1092
01:19:50.603 --> 01:19:52.538
(fire rumbling)

1093
01:20:12.625 --> 01:20:14.560
♪ ♪

1094
01:20:27.139 --> 01:20:28.774
(glass bottle clinking)

1095
01:20:31.677 --> 01:20:33.612
(man retching)

1096
01:20:37.783 --> 01:20:39.783
(man coughing)

1097
01:20:39.785 --> 01:20:41.352
(man groans)

1098
01:20:53.799 --> 01:20:55.432
(muffled grunt)

1099
01:20:55.434 --> 01:20:56.633
(shushes)

1100
01:20:56.635 --> 01:20:58.604
(panting)

1101
01:21:00.439 --> 01:21:02.373
(shushes)

1102
01:21:11.951 --> 01:21:13.519
<i>Engländer!</i>

1103
01:21:23.762 --> 01:21:24.964
(knife clatters on floor)

1104
01:21:28.434 --> 01:21:30.434
MAN (slurred):
<i>Mein Gott. Baumer.</i>

1105
01:21:30.436 --> 01:21:32.370
(man continues
speaking slurred German)

1106
01:21:36.775 --> 01:21:39.776
(Baumer choking quietly)

1107
01:21:39.778 --> 01:21:41.778
(man continues
speaking slurred German)

1108
01:21:41.780 --> 01:21:43.716
(Baumer straining quietly)

1109
01:21:49.788 --> 01:21:52.055
Baumer?

1110
01:21:52.057 --> 01:21:54.992
(man speaks slurred German)

1111
01:21:54.994 --> 01:21:56.729
Baumer?

1112
01:21:58.597 --> 01:22:00.532
Baumer?
(speaks slurred German)

1113
01:22:03.502 --> 01:22:05.535
(man grunts)

1114
01:22:05.537 --> 01:22:06.872
MAN:
Baumer!

1115
01:22:09.875 --> 01:22:12.009
- <i>Engländer!</i>
- (gunshot)

1116
01:22:12.011 --> 01:22:13.712
<i>Engländer!</i>

1117
01:22:24.590 --> 01:22:25.958
(gunshot)

1118
01:22:28.694 --> 01:22:29.826
(gunshot)

1119
01:22:29.828 --> 01:22:31.495
(grunts)

1120
01:22:31.497 --> 01:22:33.432
♪ ♪

1121
01:22:40.039 --> 01:22:42.839
(man shouts in German
in distance)

1122
01:22:42.841 --> 01:22:44.810
(gunfire continues)

1123
01:22:59.892 --> 01:23:01.860
(water rushing)

1124
01:23:04.596 --> 01:23:06.532
- (gasping)
- (gunfire continues)

1125
01:23:07.866 --> 01:23:09.835
(coughing. gasping)

1126
01:23:29.888 --> 01:23:31.857
(gasping)

1127
01:23:42.968 --> 01:23:44.903
(gasping continues)

1128
01:23:55.581 --> 01:23:57.516
♪ ♪

1129
01:24:00.119 --> 01:24:02.119
(coughing)

1130
01:24:02.121 --> 01:24:04.056
(gasping)

1131
01:24:09.962 --> 01:24:11.530
(grunts)

1132
01:24:17.836 --> 01:24:19.805
(gasping)

1133
01:24:26.612 --> 01:24:27.946
(grunting)

1134
01:24:48.033 --> 01:24:49.968
(gasping)

1135
01:24:54.640 --> 01:24:56.575
(panting)

1136
01:25:06.118 --> 01:25:09.653
(panting)

1137
01:25:09.655 --> 01:25:11.590
(water burbling gently)

1138
01:25:14.660 --> 01:25:16.059
(sighs)

1139
01:25:16.061 --> 01:25:17.996
(birds chirping)

1140
01:25:25.771 --> 01:25:27.739
(gasping)

1141
01:25:33.679 --> 01:25:35.614
♪ ♪

1142
01:25:48.093 --> 01:25:49.161
(gasps softly)

1143
01:26:00.239 --> 01:26:02.174
(grunting)

1144
01:26:22.261 --> 01:26:24.196
♪ ♪

1145
01:26:40.779 --> 01:26:42.714
(grunting)

1146
01:27:02.801 --> 01:27:05.003
(gasping grunts)

1147
01:27:13.345 --> 01:27:15.280
(gasping grunts)

1148
01:27:23.922 --> 01:27:25.857
(sobbing)

1149
01:27:41.807 --> 01:27:43.742
(panting)

1150
01:27:48.814 --> 01:27:51.750
(man singing faintly
in distance)

1151
01:28:01.827 --> 01:28:03.762
(panting)

1152
01:28:25.284 --> 01:28:27.986
(man continues singing faintly
in distance)

1153
01:28:49.308 --> 01:28:51.243
(man continues singing faintly
in distance)

1154
01:29:05.324 --> 01:29:12.430
♪ I am a poor
wayfaring stranger ♪

1155
01:29:12.432 --> 01:29:20.070
♪ I'm traveling through
this world of woe ♪

1156
01:29:20.072 --> 01:29:28.011
♪ Yet there's no sickness.
toil nor danger ♪

1157
01:29:28.013 --> 01:29:36.219
♪ In that bright land
to which I go ♪

1158
01:29:36.221 --> 01:29:44.260
♪ I'm going there
to see my father ♪

1159
01:29:44.262 --> 01:29:53.002
♪ I'm going there
no more to roam ♪

1160
01:29:53.004 --> 01:30:00.711
♪ I'm only going over Jordan ♪

1161
01:30:00.713 --> 01:30:09.185
♪ I'm only going over home ♪

1162
01:30:09.187 --> 01:30:17.461
♪ I know dark clouds
will gather round me ♪

1163
01:30:17.463 --> 01:30:26.069
♪ I know my way
is rough and steep ♪

1164
01:30:26.071 --> 01:30:34.412
♪ But golden fields
lie just before me ♪

1165
01:30:34.414 --> 01:30:43.186
♪ Where God's redeemed
shall ever sleep ♪

1166
01:30:43.188 --> 01:30:52.128
♪ I'm going home
to see my mother ♪

1167
01:30:52.130 --> 01:31:00.471
♪ And all my loved ones
who've gone on ♪

1168
01:31:00.473 --> 01:31:08.512
♪ I'm only going over Jordan ♪

1169
01:31:08.514 --> 01:31:16.487
♪ I'm only going over home ♪

1170
01:31:16.489 --> 01:31:24.495
♪ I am a poor
wayfaring stranger ♪

1171
01:31:24.497 --> 01:31:32.603
♪ I'm traveling through
this world of woe ♪

1172
01:31:32.605 --> 01:31:40.478
♪ Yet there's no sickness.
toil nor danger ♪

1173
01:31:40.480 --> 01:31:48.385
♪ In that bright land
to which I go ♪

1174
01:31:48.387 --> 01:31:56.159
♪ I'm going there
to see my father ♪

1175
01:31:56.161 --> 01:32:04.267
♪ I'm going there
no more to roam ♪

1176
01:32:04.269 --> 01:32:12.075
♪ I'm only going over Jordan ♪

1177
01:32:12.077 --> 01:32:20.684
♪ I'm only going over home. ♪

1178
01:32:20.686 --> 01:32:22.419
(applause)

1179
01:32:22.421 --> 01:32:24.655
(men chattering)

1180
01:32:24.657 --> 01:32:27.424
CAPTAIN:
D Company. move out!

1181
01:32:27.426 --> 01:32:29.493
SEYMOUR:
You all right. pal?

1182
01:32:29.495 --> 01:32:31.127
Uh. where you from?

1183
01:32:31.129 --> 01:32:32.396
GREY:
He's probably got the wind up.

1184
01:32:32.398 --> 01:32:33.531
SEYMOUR:
Well. he's not one of ours.

1185
01:32:33.533 --> 01:32:35.432
BULLEN:
He's bloody soaked.

1186
01:32:35.434 --> 01:32:38.268
GREY: Fuck it. Let's just pick
him up and take him with us.

1187
01:32:38.270 --> 01:32:40.671
(weakly):
Have to find the Devons.

1188
01:32:40.673 --> 01:32:43.574
- GREY: What's he saying?
- What's that. mate?

1189
01:32:43.576 --> 01:32:45.709
The Devons.

1190
01:32:45.711 --> 01:32:49.380
I have to find the Devons.

1191
01:32:49.382 --> 01:32:51.382
We're the Devons.

1192
01:32:51.384 --> 01:32:54.652
♪ ♪

1193
01:32:54.654 --> 01:32:57.188
- You're the Devons?
- Yes. Corp.

1194
01:32:59.224 --> 01:33:00.658
Why haven't you gone over?

1195
01:33:00.660 --> 01:33:02.325
W-We're the second wave.

1196
01:33:02.327 --> 01:33:04.160
WILLOCK:
They don't send us all at once.

1197
01:33:04.162 --> 01:33:07.163
Yeah. we're D Company.
We spent the night digging in.

1198
01:33:07.165 --> 01:33:08.666
We go last.

1199
01:33:08.668 --> 01:33:10.434
(Schofield pants)

1200
01:33:10.436 --> 01:33:12.135
Are you all right?

1201
01:33:12.137 --> 01:33:14.505
Mackenzie.
Where's Colonel Mackenzie?

1202
01:33:14.507 --> 01:33:16.607
Well. he's down at the line.

1203
01:33:16.609 --> 01:33:18.241
- Which way?
- This way.

1204
01:33:18.243 --> 01:33:20.343
We're headed up there now.

1205
01:33:20.345 --> 01:33:22.345
Oy. steady on. mate.
Where you going?

1206
01:33:22.347 --> 01:33:24.316
- (Schofield panting)
- (men murmuring)

1207
01:33:33.593 --> 01:33:35.528
♪ ♪

1208
01:33:43.669 --> 01:33:45.236
Move!

1209
01:33:48.774 --> 01:33:50.476
Let me by!

1210
01:33:54.346 --> 01:33:55.679
Let me through!

1211
01:33:55.681 --> 01:33:59.950
CAPTAIN: Remember. follow
your platoon commander.

1212
01:33:59.952 --> 01:34:02.686
Stay spread out
and watch for his orders.

1213
01:34:02.688 --> 01:34:04.488
Where is
your commanding officer?

1214
01:34:04.490 --> 01:34:06.289
He's in the holding pen.

1215
01:34:06.291 --> 01:34:09.760
CAPTAIN: Raise your signal
flags or fire the signal flares

1216
01:34:09.762 --> 01:34:12.396
when you've taken your section
of the Hun line.

1217
01:34:12.398 --> 01:34:13.664
HUTTON:
B Company. stand to.

1218
01:34:13.666 --> 01:34:15.566
Now. listen and listen well.

1219
01:34:15.568 --> 01:34:17.635
On the first mark.
A Company will advance.

1220
01:34:17.637 --> 01:34:19.803
B Company will then move
to the front line.

1221
01:34:19.805 --> 01:34:21.972
Sir. I have a message
from General Erinmore.

1222
01:34:21.974 --> 01:34:23.339
Who the fuck are you?

1223
01:34:23.341 --> 01:34:24.708
The attack has been called off.

1224
01:34:24.710 --> 01:34:26.677
General Erinmore has
called off the attack.

1225
01:34:26.679 --> 01:34:28.679
Balls. man.
We're about to go over.

1226
01:34:28.681 --> 01:34:30.414
- We've got them on the run.
- You don't.

1227
01:34:30.416 --> 01:34:31.548
Please don't
send your men over.

1228
01:34:31.550 --> 01:34:32.816
Get out of the way. Corporal!

1229
01:34:32.818 --> 01:34:34.451
These are direct orders
from army command!

1230
01:34:34.453 --> 01:34:35.686
Where is Colonel Mackenzie?!

1231
01:34:35.688 --> 01:34:38.589
Jesus Christ. man!
Go and see the captain!

1232
01:34:38.591 --> 01:34:40.691
Now. I want us up there
quickly. you understand?

1233
01:34:40.693 --> 01:34:42.426
Do you understand?!

1234
01:34:42.428 --> 01:34:44.695
- MEN: Yes. sir!
- OFFICER: Two Mills bombs per man.

1235
01:34:44.697 --> 01:34:47.296
NCOs collect flares
and signal flags.

1236
01:34:47.298 --> 01:34:49.267
- Keep to your stations.
- Oy. Oy!

1237
01:34:52.303 --> 01:34:54.272
♪ ♪

1238
01:34:57.510 --> 01:35:00.577
WRIGHT: Nine and ten section
at the ready!

1239
01:35:00.579 --> 01:35:04.448
We will advance
on the first whistle blast.

1240
01:35:04.450 --> 01:35:06.349
- 11 and 12...
- GARDNER: ...not slow down.

1241
01:35:06.351 --> 01:35:08.652
The man next to you falls.
keep moving.

1242
01:35:08.654 --> 01:35:10.688
Your orders are
to break the lines.

1243
01:35:10.690 --> 01:35:12.321
Where is the captain?

1244
01:35:12.323 --> 01:35:14.357
He's over there.

1245
01:35:14.359 --> 01:35:15.626
Keep in your section formation.

1246
01:35:15.628 --> 01:35:17.594
Sir! Sir!

1247
01:35:17.596 --> 01:35:20.864
- (sobbing)
- Captain. I have a message.

1248
01:35:20.866 --> 01:35:22.866
- This attack is called off.
- (shells firing in distance)

1249
01:35:22.868 --> 01:35:25.438
You have to stop.
You have to stop!

1250
01:35:29.374 --> 01:35:31.340
Where is Colonel Mackenzie?

1251
01:35:31.342 --> 01:35:33.311
Where is Mackenzie?!

1252
01:35:42.621 --> 01:35:44.590
(shells continue firing
in distance)

1253
01:35:51.430 --> 01:35:52.732
(grunts)

1254
01:35:55.768 --> 01:35:57.737
♪ ♪

1255
01:36:00.539 --> 01:36:02.305
Get back! Back!

1256
01:36:02.307 --> 01:36:04.074
Return to your sections! Back!

1257
01:36:04.076 --> 01:36:05.642
Hold fast!

1258
01:36:05.644 --> 01:36:07.778
RICHARDS:
Seven Platoon. one minute!

1259
01:36:07.780 --> 01:36:11.381
SCHOFIELD: Sir. I have orders
to stop this attack!

1260
01:36:11.383 --> 01:36:12.416
What?

1261
01:36:12.418 --> 01:36:14.651
Where is Colonel Mackenzie?!

1262
01:36:14.653 --> 01:36:16.620
He's further up the line.

1263
01:36:16.622 --> 01:36:18.388
- How far?
- 300 yards.

1264
01:36:18.390 --> 01:36:20.090
He's in a cut-and-cover.

1265
01:36:20.092 --> 01:36:22.793
You'll have to wait until
the first wave goes over.

1266
01:36:22.795 --> 01:36:24.730
No. No. I can't.

1267
01:36:32.605 --> 01:36:35.808
Seven Platoon. 30 seconds!

1268
01:36:41.480 --> 01:36:43.415
(explosion nearby)

1269
01:36:47.787 --> 01:36:49.686
You can't possibly
make it that way. man.

1270
01:36:49.688 --> 01:36:51.624
Are you bloody insane?

1271
01:36:55.628 --> 01:36:58.395
What the hell are you doing.
Lance Corporal?

1272
01:36:58.397 --> 01:37:00.466
No. No. no. no. no!

1273
01:37:05.805 --> 01:37:08.806
- (whistle blowing)
- (men yelling)

1274
01:37:08.808 --> 01:37:10.743
♪ ♪

1275
01:37:30.830 --> 01:37:32.765
♪ ♪

1276
01:37:52.852 --> 01:37:54.787
♪ ♪

1277
01:38:02.561 --> 01:38:04.761
Into position!

1278
01:38:04.763 --> 01:38:06.496
Get ready!

1279
01:38:06.498 --> 01:38:08.734
- Colonel Mackenzie.
- He's in there.

1280
01:38:10.502 --> 01:38:12.836
- Two minutes!
- SCHOFIELD: Let me through!

1281
01:38:12.838 --> 01:38:14.638
Hey. Hey!

1282
01:38:14.640 --> 01:38:16.440
- Let me through!
- What the hell do you think you're doing?

1283
01:38:16.442 --> 01:38:17.608
I have to get through!

1284
01:38:17.610 --> 01:38:18.976
I have to see
Colonel Mackenzie.

1285
01:38:18.978 --> 01:38:20.711
- What are you doing?
- I have to stop this attack.

1286
01:38:20.713 --> 01:38:21.945
RYLANDS:
Colonel. we've seen flares.

1287
01:38:21.947 --> 01:38:24.514
The men on the left flank have
made it to the German line.

1288
01:38:24.516 --> 01:38:26.650
- Colonel! Colonel!
- Hold him. Hold him.

1289
01:38:26.652 --> 01:38:28.886
Listen to me. Listen to me.
I have a letter.

1290
01:38:28.888 --> 01:38:30.721
I need to see
Colonel Mackenzie!

1291
01:38:30.723 --> 01:38:32.656
There's no bloody way
you're getting in there. mate.

1292
01:38:32.658 --> 01:38:33.790
RYLANDS:
Sergeant. send the next wave.

1293
01:38:33.792 --> 01:38:35.459
No!

1294
01:38:35.461 --> 01:38:37.561
SERGEANT: Second wave.
prepare yourselves!

1295
01:38:37.563 --> 01:38:39.563
- SCHOFIELD: Colonel Mackenzie!
- Concentrate everything there.

1296
01:38:39.565 --> 01:38:41.665
This attack is not to go ahead!

1297
01:38:41.667 --> 01:38:44.668
You have been ordered to stop.
You have to stop.

1298
01:38:44.670 --> 01:38:46.536
Who the hell are you?

1299
01:38:46.538 --> 01:38:48.805
Lance Corporal Schofield.
sir. 8th.

1300
01:38:48.807 --> 01:38:50.540
I have orders from
General Erinmore

1301
01:38:50.542 --> 01:38:51.675
to call off this attack.

1302
01:38:51.677 --> 01:38:53.043
You're too late.
Lance Corporal.

1303
01:38:53.045 --> 01:38:55.078
Sir. these orders
are from army command.

1304
01:38:55.080 --> 01:38:56.680
You have to read them.

1305
01:38:56.682 --> 01:38:58.482
Shall we hold back
the second wave. sir?

1306
01:38:58.484 --> 01:38:59.783
No. Major.
Hesitate now. and we lose.

1307
01:38:59.785 --> 01:39:01.551
Victory's only 500 yards away.

1308
01:39:01.553 --> 01:39:03.487
Sir. please read the letter.

1309
01:39:03.489 --> 01:39:06.490
I have heard it all before.

1310
01:39:06.492 --> 01:39:08.558
I'm not going to wait
until dusk or for fog.

1311
01:39:08.560 --> 01:39:09.860
I'm not calling back my men

1312
01:39:09.862 --> 01:39:11.528
only to send them
out there again tomorrow.

1313
01:39:11.530 --> 01:39:12.930
not when we've got
the bastards on the run.

1314
01:39:12.932 --> 01:39:14.564
This is their last stand.

1315
01:39:14.566 --> 01:39:17.000
SCHOFIELD:
The Germans planned this. sir.

1316
01:39:17.002 --> 01:39:18.802
They've been planning it
for months.

1317
01:39:18.804 --> 01:39:21.705
They want you to attack.

1318
01:39:21.707 --> 01:39:23.642
Read the letter.

1319
01:39:26.712 --> 01:39:28.647
(explosions continue
in distance)

1320
01:39:34.086 --> 01:39:36.021
(men shouting orders outside)

1321
01:39:43.595 --> 01:39:45.564
- Major?
- HEPBURN: Yes. sir?

1322
01:39:47.866 --> 01:39:50.600
- Stand them down.
- Yes. sir.

1323
01:39:50.602 --> 01:39:52.736
MACKENZIE: Call up the
orderlies. Tend the wounded.

1324
01:39:52.738 --> 01:39:54.538
Hold the line
in case they counter.

1325
01:39:54.540 --> 01:39:55.973
OFFICERS:
Yes. sir.

1326
01:39:55.975 --> 01:39:59.576
HEPBURN:
Stand down! Stand down!

1327
01:39:59.578 --> 01:40:01.311
- (sighs)
- (whistle blowing outside)

1328
01:40:01.313 --> 01:40:02.646
Stand down!

1329
01:40:02.648 --> 01:40:04.781
(whistles blowing outside)

1330
01:40:04.783 --> 01:40:07.985
- Cease fire! Cease fire!
- Stand down!

1331
01:40:07.987 --> 01:40:09.822
(Mackenzie sighs heavily)

1332
01:40:12.024 --> 01:40:14.626
I hoped today might be
a good day.

1333
01:40:16.895 --> 01:40:19.098
Hope is a dangerous thing.

1334
01:40:20.833 --> 01:40:22.733
That's it for now.
and then next week.

1335
01:40:22.735 --> 01:40:25.769
command will send
a different message.

1336
01:40:25.771 --> 01:40:27.706
"Attack at dawn."

1337
01:40:30.809 --> 01:40:32.911
There is only one way
this war ends.

1338
01:40:35.347 --> 01:40:37.516
Last man standing.

1339
01:40:42.788 --> 01:40:44.757
Have someone
see to your wounds.

1340
01:40:47.659 --> 01:40:49.895
Now fuck off. Lance Corporal.

1341
01:40:55.667 --> 01:40:56.867
OFFICER (in distance):
Bearers!

1342
01:40:56.869 --> 01:40:59.836
Stretcher bearers!

1343
01:40:59.838 --> 01:41:01.605
Bearers!

1344
01:41:01.607 --> 01:41:03.607
Stretcher bearers!

1345
01:41:03.609 --> 01:41:06.009
Well done. lad.

1346
01:41:06.011 --> 01:41:07.679
Thank you. sir.

1347
01:41:09.748 --> 01:41:12.015
Do you know where
Lieutenant Blake is. sir?

1348
01:41:12.017 --> 01:41:13.817
Blake?

1349
01:41:13.819 --> 01:41:15.719
There were two of us.

1350
01:41:15.721 --> 01:41:18.021
I was sent here
with his brother.

1351
01:41:18.023 --> 01:41:20.090
Ah.

1352
01:41:20.092 --> 01:41:21.892
Well. knowing Lieutenant Blake.

1353
01:41:21.894 --> 01:41:23.827
he would have gone over
with his men.

1354
01:41:23.829 --> 01:41:26.963
He was in the first wave.

1355
01:41:26.965 --> 01:41:28.832
How could I find him. sir?

1356
01:41:28.834 --> 01:41:31.034
You can try
the casualty clearing station

1357
01:41:31.036 --> 01:41:33.904
behind the line.

1358
01:41:33.906 --> 01:41:35.607
Otherwise...

1359
01:41:38.677 --> 01:41:40.110
Thank you. sir.

1360
01:41:40.112 --> 01:41:42.112
CAIRNS:
Major Hepburn. sir.

1361
01:41:42.114 --> 01:41:44.083
♪ ♪

1362
01:41:49.888 --> 01:41:51.857
- Keep moving. Keep moving.
- Nearly there.

1363
01:42:02.668 --> 01:42:04.002
Ow! (grunting)

1364
01:42:06.705 --> 01:42:07.773
Will I make it?

1365
01:42:10.075 --> 01:42:11.910
Will I make it?

1366
01:42:16.115 --> 01:42:18.782
- Go the fuck up.
- Clear the way.

1367
01:42:18.784 --> 01:42:20.217
Come on. quickly.

1368
01:42:20.219 --> 01:42:22.219
Get a medic!

1369
01:42:22.221 --> 01:42:25.757
Medic! Medic!

1370
01:42:33.098 --> 01:42:34.197
- Just keep moving.
- (sobbing)

1371
01:42:34.199 --> 01:42:36.133
Keep moving. keep moving.

1372
01:42:36.135 --> 01:42:37.901
That's it.

1373
01:42:37.903 --> 01:42:39.838
♪ ♪

1374
01:42:51.049 --> 01:42:53.018
(man groaning)

1375
01:43:00.125 --> 01:43:01.725
(man exhales sharply)

1376
01:43:01.727 --> 01:43:03.994
Sergeant. I have to find
Lieutenant Blake.

1377
01:43:03.996 --> 01:43:05.931
- Do you know where he is?
- No.

1378
01:43:10.736 --> 01:43:12.068
Make way for the stretchers!

1379
01:43:12.070 --> 01:43:13.770
Minor injuries
to the far field.

1380
01:43:13.772 --> 01:43:15.205
Stretchers to me.

1381
01:43:15.207 --> 01:43:17.807
Walking wounded
to the collection area.

1382
01:43:17.809 --> 01:43:20.210
Move aside to let
the stretcher bearers through.

1383
01:43:20.212 --> 01:43:21.947
(man sobbing)

1384
01:43:24.783 --> 01:43:26.718
- Move it.
- Clear the way.

1385
01:43:27.853 --> 01:43:30.020
Sir. is Lieutenant Blake here?

1386
01:43:30.022 --> 01:43:32.289
No idea.

1387
01:43:32.291 --> 01:43:35.225
Move along. Corporal.

1388
01:43:35.227 --> 01:43:38.028
If you can walk.
move to the triage area.

1389
01:43:38.030 --> 01:43:39.829
- I can't move.
- (men groaning. sobbing)

1390
01:43:39.831 --> 01:43:41.033
Help me.

1391
01:43:43.802 --> 01:43:45.068
Let me go home.

1392
01:43:45.070 --> 01:43:46.336
Lieutenant Blake!

1393
01:43:46.338 --> 01:43:48.273
I need an M.O. over here.

1394
01:43:51.777 --> 01:43:53.176
Sir. he's out.

1395
01:43:53.178 --> 01:43:55.979
Get him out of here. now.

1396
01:43:55.981 --> 01:43:59.049
Out of the bloody way.

1397
01:43:59.051 --> 01:44:01.184
SCHOFIELD:
Blake?!

1398
01:44:01.186 --> 01:44:02.852
Out of the way!

1399
01:44:02.854 --> 01:44:04.923
Has anyone seen
Lieutenant Blake?!

1400
01:44:06.825 --> 01:44:07.958
He's hemorrhaging.
Go quickly.

1401
01:44:07.960 --> 01:44:09.960
He needs a surgeon.

1402
01:44:09.962 --> 01:44:12.996
I want to be left here.

1403
01:44:12.998 --> 01:44:15.365
Tourniquet!

1404
01:44:15.367 --> 01:44:17.267
- Don't look. It's okay.
- Amputation.

1405
01:44:17.269 --> 01:44:19.169
Straight to surgery.

1406
01:44:19.171 --> 01:44:21.004
(men groaning. sobbing)

1407
01:44:21.006 --> 01:44:24.209
My leg! My leg.

1408
01:44:27.346 --> 01:44:29.279
I need some help here. quickly!

1409
01:44:29.281 --> 01:44:30.880
He's gone.

1410
01:44:30.882 --> 01:44:33.149
I can't die.

1411
01:44:33.151 --> 01:44:35.151
Don't let me fucking die.

1412
01:44:35.153 --> 01:44:37.289
- I need something now!
- I need my mum.

1413
01:44:39.992 --> 01:44:41.193
Coming through.

1414
01:44:49.167 --> 01:44:51.036
(man groaning)

1415
01:44:55.140 --> 01:44:57.274
LIEUTENANT:
All right. come on. boys.

1416
01:44:57.276 --> 01:44:59.175
He's taken one in the leg.

1417
01:44:59.177 --> 01:45:01.177
- He's lost a lot of blood.
- MAN: Sir.

1418
01:45:01.179 --> 01:45:02.613
Lieutenant Blake?

1419
01:45:02.615 --> 01:45:05.248
Yes?

1420
01:45:05.250 --> 01:45:08.318
Do you need medical assistance?

1421
01:45:08.320 --> 01:45:10.120
No. sir.

1422
01:45:10.122 --> 01:45:11.422
I'm from the 8th.

1423
01:45:11.424 --> 01:45:14.057
What the hell
are you doing here?

1424
01:45:14.059 --> 01:45:15.925
I was sent here
to deliver a message.

1425
01:45:15.927 --> 01:45:17.127
The 8th?

1426
01:45:17.129 --> 01:45:19.896
You must know my brother.

1427
01:45:19.898 --> 01:45:21.231
I was sent here with him.

1428
01:45:21.233 --> 01:45:23.201
Tom's here? Where is he?

1429
01:45:29.475 --> 01:45:31.411
It was very quick.

1430
01:45:33.479 --> 01:45:35.180
I'm sorry.

1431
01:45:41.086 --> 01:45:43.021
(metal clinking quietly)

1432
01:45:59.037 --> 01:46:01.171
BLAKE:
What's your name?

1433
01:46:01.173 --> 01:46:03.108
SCHOFIELD:
Schofield. sir.

1434
01:46:05.977 --> 01:46:08.044
I'm sorry. what?

1435
01:46:08.046 --> 01:46:09.913
It's Schofield. sir.

1436
01:46:09.915 --> 01:46:12.349
William Schofield.

1437
01:46:12.351 --> 01:46:13.919
Will.

1438
01:46:15.987 --> 01:46:17.354
Well. you need some food.

1439
01:46:17.356 --> 01:46:19.291
Get yourself to the mess tent.

1440
01:46:30.068 --> 01:46:32.003
♪ ♪

1441
01:46:34.072 --> 01:46:38.975
If I may. I'd like
to write to your mother.

1442
01:46:38.977 --> 01:46:40.912
Tell her that Tom wasn't alone.

1443
01:46:43.549 --> 01:46:45.485
(sniffles)
Of course.

1444
01:46:48.186 --> 01:46:51.020
He was...

1445
01:46:51.022 --> 01:46:52.891
He was a good man.

1446
01:46:54.727 --> 01:46:56.895
Always telling funny stories.

1447
01:46:59.432 --> 01:47:01.401
He saved my life.

1448
01:47:05.170 --> 01:47:07.139
I am glad you were with him.

1449
01:47:09.742 --> 01:47:13.176
(sniffles)

1450
01:47:13.178 --> 01:47:15.113
Thank you. Will.

1451
01:47:30.195 --> 01:47:32.130
♪ ♪

1452
01:47:52.217 --> 01:47:54.152
♪ ♪

1453
01:48:14.239 --> 01:48:16.174
♪ ♪

1454
01:48:29.254 --> 01:48:31.189
